    saetze: [
      'Begin with the map. If you know where the rivers run, your people will know which way to walk — and so will you.',
      'A name is a small history. Before you give it to a place, ask what the people there would have called it a thousand years ago.',
      'Do not explain the old days. Let a ruin stand by the road and let nobody in the story know what it was. The reader will feel the weight.',
      'The tale grows in the telling. Do not be alarmed when the short story wants to be a long one; be alarmed when it wants to be a short one and you will not let it.',
      'Write the songs. Even if you cut them later, the people of your world must have sung something on the long walks.',
      'Your hero may be small. Let him be small and tired and homesick, and let him go on anyway. That is the whole of it.',
      'Invent the language first, then the people who would speak it. A word comes with a mouth, and a mouth comes with a life.',
      'An allegory is a cage. A story is a road. If the reader wants to see himself in it, he will, but do not hang the mirror yourself.',
      'Keep a consistent inner history. A world that contradicts its own old legends is only painted cloth.',
      'Let the darkness have a price and the light a cost. A victory that costs nothing is not worth the ink.',
      'Write slowly. Twelve years is not too long for a thing that is meant to last longer than you.',
      'Put a meal in it. A fire, bread, a song at the end of the day. Comfort in a story is not weakness; it is what the danger is measured against.',
      'Do not fear the old words. Doom, wrath, fell, hallow — they are not dead, they are sleeping, and a sentence can wake them.',
      'The journey there is the book. The journey back is the chapter nobody asks for and everybody needs.',
      'When the great are busy elsewhere, let small hands do the deed. That is how the wheels of a story actually turn.',
      'Leave a road unexplored. A path going off into the trees that nobody follows is worth three that are.'
    ],
